    {
      "id": "insight-specialists-compete-on-data-workflow-depth",
      "title": "Specialist platforms compete through data workflow depth",
      "summary": "Snowflake and Databricks compete less on broad infrastructure coverage and more on integrated data, governance, warehouse, lakehouse, ML, and AI application workflows. Their signal is that enterprises will pay for fewer handoffs between data engineering, analytics, and AI delivery.",
      "implication": "Hyperscaler-style breadth needs packaged data-and-AI journeys that feel as coherent as specialist platforms, especially for governed data products and production AI launches.",
